WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:05.250
Where I come from

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:07.500
women are not allowed to speak their minds.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:09.100
As the eldest daughter

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.830
in a middle class Bengali family in Kolkata,

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:13.919
I was 'raised' in a ‘proper’ manner.

00:00:13.919 --> 00:00:15.740
I was told how to speak,

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.650
what to say and how much.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.210
Even something as simple

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:22.020
as learning how to ride a bicycle wasn’t
easy.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.380
Since I was a little girl

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.849
I always wanted to have my own bike.

00:00:25.849 --> 00:00:28.560
But it took me years to convince my parents.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.890
Finally they gave up and went to buy a bicycle
for me.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.940
I remember I was waiting patiently at home

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:37.660
and dreaming about my own bicycle.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.130
But when they came back,

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:41.520
they presented me with a sewing machine.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.720
I believe that Sewing was more appropriate

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.300
than riding a bike for a girl.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:50.000
When I came to Germany,

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.570
I could have left everything behind.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:54.470
But I still want to reach out for those women
back home,

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:57.710
who are bound by their duties and social roles.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.820
I want to show them new perspectives

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.240
and inform them about their basic rights.

